  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* B restricted to W1: is it diagonalisable with simple spectrum? *)\nBWof[u_] := BWof[u] = Transpose[LinearSolve[Transpose[W1], Transpose[W1 . Normal[Bop[u]]]]];\nus = {7/3, 11/5, -3/4, 17/6, 5/9};\nBgen = Sum[Prime[10 + k] BWof[us[[k]]], {k, Length[us]}];\nxs = Eigenvectors[Transpose[Bgen]] . W1;\neigOK = And @@ Flatten[Table[MatrixRank[{xs[[i]], xs[[i]] . Normal[Bop[uu]]}] == 1,\n     {i, Length[W1]}, {uu, {13/7, -5/2, 23/9}}]];\nGrid[{\n  {\"restriction exact\", Max[Abs[Flatten[BWof[7/3] . W1 - W1 . Normal[Bop[7/3]]]]] == 0},\n  {\"restricted B(u) commute\", Max[Abs[Flatten[Table[BWof[us[[a]]] . BWof[us[[b]]] - BWof[us[[b]]] . BWof[us[[a]]], {a, 5}, {b, 5}]]]] == 0},\n  {\"distinct eigenvalues, single B(7/3)\", Length[Union[Eigenvalues[BWof[7/3]]]]},\n  {\"distinct eigenvalues, generic combination\", Length[Union[Eigenvalues[Bgen]]]},\n  {\"15 independent covectors\", MatrixRank[xs] == Length[W1]},\n  {\"each a left eigenvector of B(u) at 3 FRESH u\", eigOK}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
